text-2xl text-foreground font-medium leading-tight","children":"Most meditation advice fails because it assumes there is only one type of mind."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-lg text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed","children":"If you tell a highly anxious person to sit in silent observation, you aren't teaching them to meditate—you are building a pressure cooker. Authentic spiritual practice recognizes that the path to stillness must match the current architecture of your nervous system and your innate mental tendencies (Vasanas)."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-lg text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed","children":"Below we categorize the four primary meditation methodologies of Sanatan Dharma by the specific temperaments they serve. One is not \"better\" than the other; they are different tools for different terrains."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-orange-600/10 border border-orange-500/20 rounded-2xl p-6 hidden md:block","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-orange-400 font-bold mb-2 uppercase text-xs tracking-widest","children":"The Core Insight"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed","children":"\"Meditation is the art of giving the mind a job it likes, until it doesn't need a job anymore.\""}]]}]]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"mb-20","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-4xl font-bold mb-10 text-center","children":"Pathways to Stillness"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8","children":[["$","article","Japa (Mantra Repetition)",{"className":"flex flex-col rounded-3xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-8 hover:border-orange-500/30 transition-all group shadow-sm hover:shadow-xl","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"w-12 h-12 rounded-2xl bg-orange-600/10 flex items-center justify-center text-orange-500 font-bold mb-6 group-hover:bg-orange-600 group-hover:text-white transition-all text-xl","children":1}],"$Ld","$Le","$Lf","$L10"]}],"$L11","$L12","